Z||000004||AL||09-02-99||08:09 PM||||well if it dies when it get' hot and then starts after 30 minutes or so, you might need a fuel pump. my trans am did this and i changed he pump and it stopped doing that. so check the fel pump.
Z||000005||fierowner||09-02-99||10:46 PM||||Same problem, new ignition modulator did jack squat for me; I've probably spent over 36 or so hours waiting on my car to cool while i was far from home and stranded; I'm so afraid to turn it off I actually let it overheat today (on accident because I didnt turn on the A/C to get the fan going) Some times i get so pissed i want to just kick the crap out of itm but i dont like broken toes.  My next modification: Cutting the floor out so i can be Fred Flintstone when it wont start.
Z||000006||87FieroGT||09-03-99||10:25 PM||||I had a similiar problem actually it was the same problem. I could run it in the morning with no problem, but if I drove around in the heat for about 30 minutes it would die on me and not start until the next day after it cooled off. I was getting fed up with it so I started to look at the wiring in the engine bay. I really didn't do anything major except reset the connections on the ignition coil. I think it may have been a bad ground, but with these things you never know. Well I hope I may have given you some info. Good luck on finding the problem.
